Subject: [PATCH 08000/11362] [outer-loop] land the exp5866 CORRIGENDUM: "every
 request got its full 4096-token budget" was wrong at K=6 (4 of 6, not 6 of 6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Straggler commit for artifacts the concurrency workflow produced after its main
body had already landed (3af9256bd, reviewed in fa81eb9f7).

THE CORRIGENDUM (results/outer_loop_exp5866_corrigendum_20260727.json). Two minor
PROSE corrections to exp5866; NO headline number changes. Published as a NEW
artifact citing the original by sha256 rather than editing it, per CLAUDE.md
never-prune, so both the original claim and its correction stay readable and the
diff is auditable.

C1 is a claim I ALSO repeated to the operator. Published: "PASS at K=4 AND at
K=6 ... EVERY request got its FULL 4096-token budget." What the raw rows
(generator_concurrency_5866/fixprice.json candidates[0].cells[1]) actually say:
requests 0-3 returned generated_tokens=4096 with stop_type='limit', but requests
4 and 5 returned 898 and 877 tokens with stop_type='eos', truncated=false -- a
NATURAL finish, not the budget. So 4 of 6 hit the budget and 2 of 6 stopped early
on their own. The SUBSTANCE is unaffected: no 500s, no deaths, and critically no
pool_exhaustion_limit -- an 'eos' stop is the model finishing, not the pool
truncating it, which is the distinction the stop_taxonomy witness exists to make.
But "every" was not true and is now on the record as not true.

WHAT IS EXPLICITLY NOT CORRECTED, quoted from the artifact: exp5866's headline
conclusions all stand -- the VRAM fit (max error 0.19%), the mode A/B/C taxonomy,
context being the cheap axis (~0.025 MiB/cell vs ~207 MiB/slot), and the
recommendation to raise n_ctx to 81920.

Also landed: the rebuilt first-win artifact + its build script, the corrigendum's
build script, and the analyser index entry.

Verify: adversarial_verify `Scanned 1 artifact(s); 0 flagged.` ·
artifact_freshness_lint OK · determination_preservation_lint OK · ruff check and
format clean on all touched files.

No SUBMITTED_* flag moved. MAX_ACTIONS (400) and SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE (None)
untouched. Nothing submitted to ARC or Kaggle.

